  "name": "provider-api-call-dedup",
  "description": "Use when a provider scan is slow, times out, or trips rate limits (429, throttling, Retry-After), when the same request URL appears many times in a debug log, when an asset's fields look like they cost one API call per scanned asset, or when auditing any provider under providers/ for redundant per-asset API traffic. Applies to aws, azure, gcp, k8s, okta and any other provider, since the resource cache and init dispatch are shared machinery.",
